%description:
Tests that a FIN does not restart a running retransmission timer (RFC 6298
section 5.1: "if the timer is not running, start it running"). The tester
removes the data segment of t=1. The application closes at t=1.5, so the FIN
goes while the data is in flight. The retransmission comes 3 s (the initial
RTO) after the data segment, at t=4; when the FIN restarted the timer, it came
at t=4.5.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 1000"
*.cli_app.tClose=1.5s
*.tcptester.script="a3 delete"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[1.001 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: A 1:1001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 # deleting
cli_tcp: ESTABLISHED --> FIN_WAIT_1  (on CLOSE)
[1.501 A004] A.1000 > B.2000: A F ack 501 win 16384 
[4.001 A005] A.1000 > B.2000: A F 1:1001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 
srv_tcp: ESTABLISHED --> CLOSE_WAIT  (on RCV_FIN)
[4.003 B002] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 1002 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
